Classifies all light two-wheelers, three-wheelers, and quadricycles:
- L1: Two-wheelers with maximum design speed <= 50 km/h (displacement <= 50 cc for thermal or <= 4 kW for electric engines);
- L2: Three-wheelers with maximum design speed <= 50 km/h (displacement <= 50 cc or <= 4 kW);
- L3: Two-wheeled motorcycles with speed > 50 km/h (displacement > 50 cc);
- L4: Motorcycles with an asymmetrical sidecar, speed > 50 km/h;
- L5: Symmetrically arranged three-wheelers (auto-rickshaws), speed > 50 km/h. Subdivided into L5-M (Passenger Carrier) and L5-N (Goods Carrier);
- L6: Light quadricycles with unladen mass <= 350 kg, speed <= 45 km/h, max power <= 4 kW;
- L7: Heavy quadricycles with unladen mass <= 400 kg (or <= 550 kg for goods transport), max speed <= 45 km/h, max continuous power <= 15 kW.

Classifies all four-wheeled motor vehicles designed and constructed for carrying passengers:
- M1: Vehicles comprising not more than 8 seats in addition to the driver's seat (passenger cars);
- M2: Vehicles comprising 9 or more seats in addition to the driver's seat, with a Gross Vehicle Weight (GVW) not exceeding 5 tonnes;
- M3: Vehicles comprising 9 or more seats in addition to the driver's seat, with a Gross Vehicle Weight (GVW) exceeding 5 tonnes (commercial buses).

Classifies all four-wheeled motor vehicles designed and constructed for carrying goods:
- N1: Vehicles used for the carriage of goods, having a Gross Vehicle Weight (GVW) not exceeding 3.5 tonnes;
- N2: Vehicles used for the carriage of goods, having a Gross Vehicle Weight (GVW) exceeding 3.5 tonnes but not exceeding 12 tonnes;
- N3: Vehicles used for the carriage of goods, having a Gross Vehicle Weight (GVW) exceeding 12 tonnes.

Under India-specific CMVR and AIS alignment, towed trailers are designated as Category T (as opposed to Category O internationally):
- T1: Trailers and semi-trailers having a maximum weight not exceeding 0.75 tonnes;
- T2: Trailers and semi-trailers having a maximum weight exceeding 0.75 tonnes but not exceeding 3.5 tonnes;
- T3: Trailers and semi-trailers having a maximum weight exceeding 3.5 tonnes but not exceeding 10 tonnes;
- T4: Trailers and semi-trailers having a maximum weight exceeding 10 tonnes;
- T5: Semi-trailers intended to be drawn by a three-wheeled haulage tractor.
